<details><summary><strong>Terminal: Slurm jobs, cluster modules, this app's image in jobs</strong></summary>

In this session's terminal:

- `sbatch`, `srun`, `squeue` ... are the cluster's own; jobs start with the cluster's environment, not the app's.
- `ood-run -c 8 --mem 32G -- COMMAND` runs a command as a job in this app's image; `ood-shell -c 4` opens one interactively.
- `ood-host` opens a shell on this node outside the app, inside this session's job (all cluster modules work there).
- `module avail` lists the cluster modules tested to work inside this app; `module load NAME` adds their commands.

In Slurm jobs and cluster shells: `module use /ijc/PUBLIC/DATA/images/ood/modulefiles`, then `module load ood/jupyter` or `ood/rstudio` (`module avail ood` lists the versions). More: `/ijc/PUBLIC/DATA/images/ood/README.md`.
</details>
